# Waste Monkey

## Lore

Also called the Shovel-Paw Monkey: a ground-dwelling primate that may be the mutated descendant of escaped zoo animals, a product of genetic manipulation, or a creature from another dimension. It looks much like a Spider Monkey half again as large, with a stub of a tail, spade-like hooves for hands that dig out burrows, grubs and roots, and prehensile feet. It moves on its knuckles, feet swinging below, and is remarkably nimble and quick.

Waste Monkeys live in lodges of 3-10 mated pairs, raising their young together in caves and burrows dug under boulders, tree roots or the wrecks of vehicles left by adventurers who died in the Waste. The females tend the young and the burrow; the males gather food and fight off predators. Curious, clever and playful, they peer out from the edge of the Waste and raid the Clarkdale Confederacy in pairs for food. Caught and taken away, they make fine pets (miners, vagabonds, swindlers and thieves prize them, since one can be told to fetch a wallet or distract the guards), though one that sees the Waste again is likely to bolt for it.

They like humanoids, especially humans, human-like D-Bees, mutants and mutant animals, and fight fiercely for a friend or lodge-mate, though as S.D.C. creatures they prefer to lure danger away or into the path of a bigger animal. Predators, canines and felines above all, and the people who catch them for pets or resale are their enemies. Most live in the Waste and do poorly in cold climates.

## GM Notes

The book says the Waste Monkey makes an excellent G.M.''s character and may be offered to a player, who then plays an animal-like creature with a young child''s intelligence and a teenager''s cunning; it is not suited to every campaign or player. Size 2-3 feet (0.6-0.9 m) tall standing fully erect, weight 13-18 lbs (5.9-8 kg), life span 25-30 years. Allies: none as such, though they like Thumpers (which keep no pets) and quickly befriend humans and D-Bees who feed them and treat them well.

The book''s modifiers to some secondary skills are not applied by the sheet: Basic Mechanics -10%, Gymnastics +5%, Palming +2%, Play Musical Instrument -10%, Sign Language -10%, Swimming -15%.

The creature row Waste Monkey in the bestiary is the same entry for use as an NPC.
